  "text": "Conditional Probability Conditional Probability The probability that event A occurs given that event B has already occurred is called the conditional probability of A given B. Symbolically, this is written as P(A|B). The probability it rains on Monday given that it rained on Sunday would be written as P(Rain on Monday | Rain on Sunday).",
